Interpretation:

The find() method scans records one by one until it finds the required pass ID. As the number of records increases, the search may take more time.

Its worst-case time complexity is O(n), where n is the number of records. Alternative Concept and Complexity Analysis If the file is loaded once into a HashMap, each pass ID can be used as a key. Method Time for q searches Memory File scanning O(q × n) O(1) extra memory HashMap O(n + q) average O(n)

Conclusion:

A file scan uses less extra memory but takes more time for repeated searches. A HashMap uses additional memory but provides faster average search performance.
